{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:24:39.273Z","ordinal":16327,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0aa80-3aab-7313-9603-edf7533a1570","turn_id":"01a0b02e-7a81-7bf1-8757-64a5247d115a","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0b3476aa27839743016aac1443fe4887d0aaf9103471e4115a","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Findings:\n\n- The action change is important: it makes the version-PR action default to `callisto version --refresh-lockfiles`, preventing the exact `Cargo.lock` drift that caused a clean-worktree release failure. Its current description is needlessly long; I’ll shorten it while retaining the behavior.\n- The Markdown changes are relevant: license-boundary corrections and the sibling-gap rule directly address the release incident’s “patch one symptom” pattern.\n- Entire-search was installed as a managed integration on September 11 across Claude, Codex, Gemini, OpenCode, and agent paths. The files have the same timestamp and an `ENTIRE-MANAGED` marker; it was not created by this recovery work. History points to the prior Entire setup/hardening work, though the indexed transcript does not identify the exact creating command.\n\n"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1789662276019,"completed_at_ms":1789662279273}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:24:39.275Z","ordinal":16328,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0b3476aa27839743016aac1443fe4887d0aaf9103471e4115a","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Findings:\n\n- The action change is important: it makes the version-PR action default to `callisto version --refresh-lockfiles`, preventing the exact `Cargo.lock` drift that caused a clean-worktree release failure. Its current description is needlessly long; I’ll shorten it while retaining the behavior.\n- The Markdown changes are relevant: license-boundary corrections and the sibling-gap rule directly address the release incident’s “patch one symptom” pattern.\n- Entire-search was installed as a managed integration on September 11 across Claude, Codex, Gemini, OpenCode, and agent paths. The files have the same timestamp and an `ENTIRE-MANAGED` marker; it was not created by this recovery work. History points to the prior Entire setup/hardening work, though the indexed transcript does not identify the exact creating command.\n\n"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b02e-7a81-7bf1-8757-64a5247d115a","create_time":1789662267.598891,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:24:43.823Z","ordinal":16329,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0b3476aa27839743016aac144741a087d0ae4a460253c1bc4e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_cbLChsgpbTBzqwnOmtXKmByo","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.gitignore\\n@@\\n .claude/worktrees/\\n+.playwright-mcp/\\n mutants.out/\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml\\n@@\\n-    description: 'Version command; defaults to callisto version --refresh-lockfiles. `--emit-decision <decision_path>` is always appended, so a replacement command must also accept it (typically by wrapping `callisto version` itself). `--refresh-lockfiles` keeps the workspace-member version fields in Cargo.lock (and other ecosystem lockfiles) in sync with the just-bumped manifests -- without it, the next plain `cargo build`/`install` on the release commit rewrites the lockfile itself and fails the release-trust clean-worktree check.'\\n+    description: 'Version command; defaults to callisto version --refresh-lockfiles. Callisto appends --emit-decision <decision_path>.'\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst r = await tools.apply_patch(patch);\ntext(typeof r === \"string\" ? r : JSON.stringify(r));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b02e-7a81-7bf1-8757-64a5247d115a","create_time":1789662267.598891}}}
